Subject: [PATCH] demux_mkv: widen subtitle preroll to 10s and enable on every seek

PGS/VobSub bitmap subtitles only carry the "show" command at the start of a
line. The default subtitle preroll window is 1 second, and in "index" mode it
is only used when the file carries a duration index. Seeking into the middle
of a longer line therefore skips that line's bitmap packet entirely, and
nothing is displayed until the next line's packet arrives.

Enable the preroll unconditionally and widen the window to 10 seconds, which
is already the default for the duration-index path
(subtitle_preroll_secs_index). This only costs extra demuxing at seek time:
audio and video packets in the preroll window are dropped in the demuxer and
never reach the decoders.

---
--- a/demux/demux_mkv.c
+++ b/demux/demux_mkv.c
@@ -258,8 +258,13 @@
     },
     .size = sizeof(struct demux_mkv_opts),
     .defaults = &(const struct demux_mkv_opts){
-        .subtitle_preroll = 2,
-        .subtitle_preroll_secs = 1.0,
+        // Preroll on every seek (not only when the file carries a duration
+        // index) and widen the window from 1s to 10s. PGS/VobSub bitmaps carry
+        // the "show" command only at the start of a line, so a 1s window misses
+        // the current line whenever the seek lands in the middle of it: nothing
+        // is shown until the next line's packet arrives.
+        .subtitle_preroll = 1,
+        .subtitle_preroll_secs = 10.0,
         .subtitle_preroll_secs_index = 10.0,
         .probe_start_time = true,
         .crop_compat = true,
